# Rule 2, at the level of names (jlt-tool): a function template's body may
# use, on a value whose type depends on a template parameter, only an operation
# some requirement of its constraints names, the constraints followed through
# their concepts; the DECLARED constraints only, a requires-expression or
# concept test inside the body is not one (by decision: the rule set stays
# simple and the code names what it uses).  A sanity check, not a proof: silent where it
# cannot read a constraint.  What it does not see is listed at the check in
# tool/jlt_tool.cpp.
